    | 219 | 1 | Synergy Test: Bottleneck+Dilated(d=5)+Double-Step | Krono I | 123 | 82.80 |\n| 213 | 1 | Ultimate Baseline: Wide+Residual+Double-Step | Krono I | 120 | 67.20 |\n| 212 | 1 | Ultimate Synergy v2: Wide+Bottleneck+Double-Step | Krono I | 119 | 82.80 |\n| 207 | 1 | Standard Synergy: Bottleneck + Dilated CNN (No FE) | Krono I | 116 | 73.10 |\n| 204 | 1 | Ultimate Synergy: Wide+Bottleneck+Dilated CNN (No FE) | Krono I | 115 | 72.50 |\n| 202 | 1 | Replication: Bottleneck Wide CNN (No FE) | Krono I | 114 | 77.20 |\n| 199 | 1 | Ablation: Bottleneck Ratio Sweep on Wide CNN SOTA | Krono I | 113 | 75.90 |\n| 188 | 1 | Paper Recovery 2: Bottleneck Blocks on Standard-Width CNN | Krono I | 105 | 75.50 |\n| 187 | 1 | Paper Recovery 1: Wide CNN SOTA Baseline Replication | Krono I | 105 | 63.50 |\n| 183 | 1 | Synergy Test: Bottleneck Blocks + Dilated CNN (d=4) | Krono I | 103 | 73.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 6 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-6, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**krono/double_step_synergy.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\nfrom bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\nclass DoubleStepSynergyNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Standard-Width, Dilated CNN with Bottleneck Blocks\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n        \n        # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        \n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        rnn_state_1, _ = lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n        rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, cnn_out)\n        new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final\
    \ MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
