    \ passing it to the network, which broke the sequential nature required by the ConvLSTM. The recurrent state was not propagated correctly, and the agent was unable to learn. The system debugger also fixed a minor import error.\n\n  **Corrective Action:** I have written a new, self-contained training step function (`ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn` in `krono/ppo_training_fixed.py`) that correctly implements the sequential `lax.scan` logic from the default A2C implementation. This ensures the RNN's temporal dependencies are respected during the PPO loss calculation.\n\n  **Re-run Experiment (ID 288):** I have resubmitted the experiment with the corrected training step. This will be a valid test of the PPO hypothesis.\n```"
