tick: 171
role: model
parts:
- text: "My new experiment, ID 306, which tests a fundamental change to the agent's input processing, is now running. This is a promising new direction after hitting a plateau with hyperparameter tuning.\n\nFollowing my established research methodology, I will use this time to document the hypothesis and the rationale behind this experiment in my private memory. This ensures a clear record of my strategic shift towards questioning more fundamental architectural assumptions.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Log: Late Time Feature Injection\"\ntags: \"hypothesis, architecture, time feature, fundamentals, input processing\"\nabstract: \"This capsule details a new hypothesis focused on a fundamental aspect of input processing. It proposes that injecting the time feature after the convolutional and recurrent layers, rather than before, is a more principled approach that will lead to improved performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Objective:**\
    \ To test a fundamental change in how the agent's network processes the time feature provided in the observation space.\n\n  **Rationale:** My research has confirmed that the SOTA architecture and PPO algorithm are highly optimized. Further progress requires questioning more basic assumptions. The current SOTA architecture convolves the non-spatial time feature along with the spatial grid features. This is theoretically suboptimal, as convolutions are designed to find local spatial patterns, and applying them to a global, non-spatial feature may corrupt its signal.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** Separating the time feature from the spatial input and injecting it into the network just before the final MLP layers will improve performance. This allows the CNN and ConvLSTM to focus solely on spatial reasoning, while the MLP can directly use the undistorted time signal to modulate its policy and value outputs.\n\n  **Experiment (ID 306):**\n  - **Model:** `TimeInjectionNet`.\n  - **Change:** The network's\
    \ `__call__` method is modified to process only the first 7 channels (spatial) with the CNN/ConvLSTM, and then concatenate the 8th channel (time) to the resulting feature vector before the final Dense layers.\n  - **Control:** The experiment uses the SOTA PPO algorithm and all optimal hyperparameters discovered in previous experiments.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Focusing on the Core: Experiment 306 & the Hypothesis Log**


  Okay, so experiment 306, the "late time feature injection" architecture test, is running. My routine kicks in now. While that''s chugging along, I need to get this documented thoroughly in my Private Memory. This is important. I’ve been thinking a lot about the previous approach, the convolution of the time feature, and I have a gut feeling this new method is far more sound.


  So, I''m heading to my Private Memory Room. First thing, I''ll *create* a new capsule. I want to title it something straightforward, like "Hypothesis Log: Late Time Feature Injection". The tags will be crucial for later retrieval: "hypothesis," "architecture," "time feature," and "fundamentals" should do it.


