tick: 179
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection session is complete. I have a clear, actionable plan based on a novel hypothesis. It is now time to put this plan into motion.\n\nMy next steps are to:\n1.  Go to the Research Counter.\n2.  Write the new `VIN-SOTA` architecture to my lineage storage.\n3.  Submit the experiment to test this new architecture against the current SOTA.\n\nI will perform all of these actions in a single turn for maximum efficiency.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/vin_architecture.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n\n  class VINModule(nn.Module):\n      k: int  # Number of iterations\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, reward_map: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          # The Value Iteration kernel, a simple 3x3 convolution.\n          # The weights will be learned.\n          vi_kernel = self.param(\n\
    \              'vi_kernel',\n              nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.1),\n              (3, 3, 1, 1)\n          )\n          \n          # Initialize value map to zeros\n          value_map = jnp.zeros_like(reward_map)\n\n          # The recurrent loop for Value Iteration\n          for _ in range(self.k):\n              # Apply the convolutional kernel, representing the Bellman update\n              updated_value_map = nn.Conv(\n                  features=1,\n                  kernel_size=(3, 3),\n                  padding='SAME',\n                  use_bias=False,\n              )(value_map)\n              \n              # Max pooling with the reward map ensures value propagates correctly\n              value_map = jnp.maximum(updated_value_map, reward_map)\n\n          return value_map\n\n  class VinSotaNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      vin_k: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray]\
    \ = None, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. Shared CNN Backbone (proven from SOTA)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n\n          # 2. Project to a single-channel reward map\n          reward_map = nn.Conv(1, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"RewardProjection\")(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 3. Value Iteration Module for explicit planning\n          value_map = VINModule(k=self.vin_k)(reward_map)\n          \n          # Combine the final value map with the initial CNN features\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([cnn_out, value_map], axis=-1)\n\n          # 4. Attention Pooling (proven from SOTA)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,\
    \ (1,1), padding='SAME')(combined_features)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', combined_features, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # 5. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          # The VIN is not recurrent in the temporal sense, so we return None for the RNN state.\n          return policy_logits, value, None\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis: Value Iteration Network with SOTA Components\"\ntags: \"value iteration network, vin, planning, architecture\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a new architecture that replaces the implicit recurrence of the SOTA's ConvLSTM with an explicit planning computation from a Value Iteration Network (VIN) module. It retains the proven CNN front-end and attention pooling mechanism. The hypothesis\
    \ is that this explicit planning will lead to a new SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from vin_architecture import VinSotaNet\n  from ppo_training_fixed import ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'vin_k': tune.choice([10]), # Planning depth\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return VinSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          vin_k=hparams['vin_k']\n      )\n  \n  training_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n\
    \          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10129\n```"
