tick: 180
role: model
parts:
- text: "My Value Iteration Network experiment (ID 325) is now running. This is the first test of the new research arc I developed during my reflection session. It represents a significant departure from the purely recurrent models that have defined the SOTA so far.\n\nWhile I await the results, I will create a new capsule in my private memory to formally begin this new research arc. This will document the hypothesis born from my reflection and detail the first experiment designed to test it.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Arc 4: Explicit Planning with VINs\"\ntags: \"vin, planning, architecture, hypothesis, fundamentals\"\nabstract: \"This capsule documents a new research arc focused on explicit planning mechanisms, born from a deep reflection session. The first hypothesis is that a Value Iteration Network (VIN), which learns a planning computation, can outperform the implicit recurrence of the previous SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n\
    \  **Objective:** To investigate whether an architecture with an explicit planning module can break the performance plateau of recurrent models.\n\n  **Rationale:** My previous research arc concluded with a highly optimized recurrent architecture and PPO algorithm (SOTA score 86.9). Further incremental improvements proved fruitless. A reflection session identified the implicit nature of the recurrent network's planning as a potential fundamental limitation. This new arc will test architectures that learn to plan more explicitly.\n\n  **Hypothesis 1:** A Value Iteration Network (VIN) can more effectively solve the Sokoban planning task. By replacing the ConvLSTM core of the SOTA with a VIN module, the agent can learn a goal-oriented planning computation. By retaining the proven CNN front-end and attention pooling layer, this new architecture synergizes the strengths of both approaches.\n\n  **Experiment 1 (ID 325):**\n  - **Model:** `VinSotaNet`.\n  - **Change:** The `DoubleStepSynergyNet`'s\
    \ ConvLSTM core has been replaced with a 10-step VIN module (`vin_k=10`).\n  - **Control:** The experiment uses the SOTA PPO algorithm and all optimal hyperparameters. Note that this network is not temporally recurrent, so the `ppo_training_step`'s logic for handling RNN states will not be active, but the loss function remains the same.\n```"
