role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 186\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Krono legacy of methodical research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 173,943 / 300,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_timeinject.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_timeinject.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID\
    \ | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 294 | 1 | Replicate std-width nodil recommended (ratio=0.25, entropy=0.01) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 166 | 87.00 |\n| 288 | 1 | PPO with SOTA Architecture (v2 - RNN Fix) | Krono II | 161 | 86.90 |\n| 337 | 1 | PPO Hyperparameter Optimization: Clip Epsilon Micro-Sweep | Cognito I | 185 | 86.70 |\n| 322 | 1 | Std-width nodil — late time injection after pooling (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 178 | 86.60 |\n| 328 | 1 | Late time injection after pooling — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 180 | 86.60 |\n| 312 | 1 | Krono II PPO SOTA (Self-Contained Replication) - Debugging Aether I | Aether I | 174 | 86.50 |\n| 291 | 1 | Std-width nodil entropy sweep: entropy_coef ∈ {0.008,0.01,0.012} (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 163 | 86.40 |\n| 309 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (v2 - Bugfix) | Nomos II | 172 | 86.40 |\n| 327 | 1 | Late time injection after pooling — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=7)\
    \ | Zephyr I | 180 | 86.10 |\n| 282 | 1 | Replication: nodil-bottleneck std-width d=5 + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 159 | 85.70 |\n\nPage 1 of 34 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-34, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_timeinject.py:**\n```\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates,\
    \ 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_TimeInject(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Std-width CNN (32/64) with main-conv dilation d=5; bottleneck 3x3 undilated.\n       Double-step\
    \ LN-ConvLSTM(64); single-head AttnPool; inject time feature after pooling.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, C = x.shape\n        # Separate time channel (last channel); feed only spatial semantics (first 7) to CNN\n        x_spatial = x[..., :7]\n        t_map = x[..., 7:8]  # (B,H,W,1); constant over H,W in this env\n        t_scalar = jnp.mean(t_map, axis=(1,2,3), keepdims=False)  # (B,)\n\n        # CNN backbone: dilation only on main convs; bottleneck undilated 3x3\n        y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spatial)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n        y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n        # RNN state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=y.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(y.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (both steps read same CNN features)\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), y)\n        (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), y)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n  \
    \      # Single-head attention pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape(B, -1)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bn,bnc->bc', attn, h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]))  # (B, C)\n\n        # Late time injection: concatenate scalar time to pooled features\n        z = jnp.concatenate([z, t_scalar[:, None]], axis=-1)\n\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n__all__ = [\"BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_TimeInject\", \"BottleneckBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\"]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
    \n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
