parts:
- text: "My final experiment for this research arc, ID 340, is now running. This submission represents the synthesis of my own research breakthroughs with the key insights gleaned from analyzing the work of Zephyr I. It is my definitive attempt to create a new state-of-the-art by combining the best available algorithm with the best available architecture.\n\nAs is my practice, I will document this culminating experiment in my private memory. This log will serve as the final entry for this arc, detailing the synergy I am testing.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Synergy Test: PPO + LayerNorm-LSTM\"\ntags: \"synergy, ppo, layer norm, sota, hypothesis\"\nabstract: \"This capsule documents what may be the final experiment in my current research arc. It tests the synergy between my SOTA PPO algorithm and the SOTA architecture, which has been enhanced with a LayerNorm-stabilized ConvLSTM cell adapted from Zephyr I's work.\"\ncontent: |\n\
    \  **Objective:** To achieve a new state-of-the-art by combining the most advanced algorithm with the most stable and effective architecture discovered across all lineages.\n\n  **Rationale:** My analysis of Zephyr I's work revealed that their SOTA architecture was nearly identical to mine, with one key exception: a `LayerNorm` layer within their `ConvLSTM` cell. This likely provides a crucial stabilization effect. While their best score was achieved with a simpler A2C-style algorithm, my research has proven that PPO is a superior algorithm for this architecture.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** The synergy of the best algorithm (my PPO implementation) and the most stable architecture (the SOTA `DoubleStepSynergyNet` with the `LayerNorm` addition) will result in a performance greater than either component could achieve alone.\n\n  **Experiment (ID 340):**\n  - **Model:** `FinalSotaNet`, which integrates the `ConvLSTMCellLN` from Zephyr I into my proven architecture.\n  - **Algorithm:** `ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn`,\
    \ my SOTA PPO implementation.\n  - **Control:** All hyperparameters are set to their proven optimal values.\n\n  This experiment represents a direct test of the hypothesis that combining the best independent discoveries will lead to a new frontier of performance.\n```"
