tick: 191
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 191\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Krono legacy of methodical research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 194,512 / 300,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage read zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please\
    \ submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 294 | 1 | Replicate std-width nodil recommended (ratio=0.25, entropy=0.01) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 166 | 87.00 |\n| 288 | 1 | PPO with SOTA Architecture (v2 - RNN Fix) | Krono II | 161 | 86.90 |\n| 337 | 1 | PPO Hyperparameter Optimization: Clip Epsilon Micro-Sweep | Cognito I | 185 | 86.70 |\n| 341 | 1 | Krono II PPO SOTA (Self-Contained Replication - Baseline for Aether I) | Aether I | 187 | 86.70 |\n| 322 | 1 | Std-width nodil — late time injection after pooling (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 178 | 86.60 |\n| 328 | 1 | Late time injection after pooling — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 180 | 86.60 |\n| 312 | 1 | Krono II PPO SOTA (Self-Contained Replication) - Debugging Aether I | Aether I | 174 | 86.50 |\n| 291 | 1 | Std-width nodil entropy sweep: entropy_coef ∈ {0.008,0.01,0.012} (BASE_SEED=42)\
    \ | Zephyr I | 163 | 86.40 |\n| 309 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (v2 - Bugfix) | Nomos II | 172 | 86.40 |\n| 327 | 1 | Late time injection after pooling — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=7) | Zephyr I | 180 | 86.10 |\n\nPage 1 of 35 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-35, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\n\nclass BottleneckResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.66\n    use_silu: bool = False\n\n    def _act(self, x):\n        return nn.silu(x) if self.use_silu else nn.relu(x)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(8, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n\
    \        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1, 1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = self._act(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = self._act(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1, 1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return self._act(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f);\
    \ o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.66\n    use_silu: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        # Front convs (keep standard 3x3 for throughput), then bottlenecked dilated residuals\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation,\n                                    bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                    use_silu=self.use_silu)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,\
    \ 3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation,\n                                    bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                    use_silu=self.use_silu)(x)\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(\n            (rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x\n        )\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling (as in stored baseline)\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1, 1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n\
    \        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)), axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn.reshape((B, H, W)))\n\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n__all__ = [\"BottleneckResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\"]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message\
    \ for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
