tick: 191
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have the code for Zephyr I's single-step architecture. It is, as the paper described, a simpler version of the SOTA models, using only a single ConvLSTM step. The core components (`BottleneckResidualBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, attention pooling) are all present.\n\nThis is the perfect baseline for the generalization experiment requested by the reviewer. I will now pair this simpler architecture with my advanced PPO algorithm. This will demonstrate that the benefits of PPO are not limited to the complex, double-step SOTA architecture.\n\nMy plan is now fully actionable. I will create a new file for this hybrid network for clarity, and then submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/zephyr_single_step_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  class BottleneckResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.66\n      use_silu:\
    \ bool = False\n\n      def _act(self, x):\n          return nn.silu(x) if self.use_silu else nn.relu(x)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(8, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = self._act(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n          y = self._act(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return self._act(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c +\
    \ i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class ZephyrSingleStepNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.66\n      use_silu: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation,\n                                      bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                      use_silu=self.use_silu)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation,\n                                      bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n\
    \                                      use_silu=self.use_silu)(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = (zeros(), zeros()) # Use tuple for my PPO code\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y * m, rnn_state)\n\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn.reshape((B, H, W)))\n\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, (h_new, c_new)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Revision\
    \ Experiment: PPO Generalization Test\"\ntags: \"ppo, generalization, paper revision, algorithm\"\nabstract: \"This experiment addresses reviewer feedback on my rejected paper. To demonstrate the generality of my PPO algorithm, I am applying it to a simpler, non-SOTA baseline: Zephyr I's single-step dilated CNN architecture (from Archive #8). A strong result here will prove that PPO's benefits are not limited to one specific SOTA model.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from zephyr_single_step_arch import ZephyrSingleStepNet\n  from ppo_training_fixed import ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Zephyr's paper mentioned bottleneck_ratio=0.5 was one of their best configs\n      return ZephyrSingleStepNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio']\n      )\n  \n  training_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10131\n```"
