parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 193\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Krono legacy of methodical research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 201,117 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 62 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Paper Revision Experiment: PPO Generalization Test' (ID: 347) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 74.7\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.752, 0.686, 0.752, 0.796]\nMean: 0.747, Std: 0.039\nBest trial: 4 (0.796)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 5.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.500000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 347\n\n## Summary\n\
    **Success** - Fixed missing import error that was causing the code to crash immediately. The fixed code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed with `NameError: name 'jax' is not defined` at line 64 of `storage/krono/zephyr_single_step_arch.py`. The file imported `jax.numpy as jnp` and `flax.linen as nn` but was missing the main `jax` import needed for `jax.tree.map()`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. **Copied problematic classes**: Copied `ZephyrSingleStepNet`, `BottleneckResidualBlock`, and `ConvLSTMCellLN` from the lineage file into `submission_v2.py`\n2. **Added missing import**: Added `import jax` to the submission file  \n3. **Maintained existing imports**: Kept the working import for `ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn` from the lineage\n4. **Added required imports**: Added the necessary JAX and Flax imports that were missing\n\nThe fix ensures that when `jax.tree.map(lambda y: y * m, rnn_state)` is called at line 64 of the network architecture, the `jax` module is\
    \ properly imported and available.\n\n## Status\nThe fixed submission (v2) has been running for over 2 minutes without crashes, indicating the import error has been resolved. The evaluation system is now able to execute the code successfully.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\n\n# Fixed version of the classes from zephyr_single_step_arch.py with proper jax import\nclass BottleneckResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.66\n    use_silu: bool = False\n\n    def _act(self, x):\n        return nn.silu(x) if self.use_silu else nn.relu(x)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n    \
    \    mid = max(8, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = self._act(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n        y = self._act(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(y)\n        return self._act(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass ZephyrSingleStepNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features:\
    \ int\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.66\n    use_silu: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation,\n                                    bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                    use_silu=self.use_silu)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation,\n                                    bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                    use_silu=self.use_silu)(x)\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = (zeros(),\
    \ zeros()) # Use tuple for my PPO code\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1).astype(x.dtype))\n            # Fixed: now jax is properly imported\n            rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y * m, rnn_state)\n\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn.reshape((B, H, W)))\n\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, (h_new, c_new)\n\n# Import the working function from lineage \nfrom ppo_training_fixed import ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef':\
    \ tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Zephyr's paper mentioned bottleneck_ratio=0.5 was one of their best configs\n    return ZephyrSingleStepNet(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio']\n    )\n\ntraining_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 10131\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n\
    ```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10131 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps\
    \ per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.40 | 1.88 | 2.36 | 8.22 | 4.59 | 6.09 | 10.42 | 8.41 | 10.15 | 11.53 | 12.48\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.071 | 0.111 | 0.556 | 0.286 | 0.385 | 0.737 | 0.571 | 0.714 | 0.828 | 0.905\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1330s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.752\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.752\nTraining time: 1345s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\n\
    Network output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.40 | 0.88 | 2.38 | 4.68 | 7.69 | 6.76 | 4.55 | 10.60 | 9.93 | 12.39 | 11.01\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.091 | 0.267 | 0.533 | 0.438 | 0.267 | 0.762 | 0.700 | 0.900 | 0.792\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1420s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.686\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.686\nTraining time: 1436s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.13 | 1.90 | 7.70 | 9.46 | 9.71 | 9.20 | 10.84 | 10.44\
    \ | 8.13 | 8.38 | 11.90\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.100 | 0.500 | 0.667 | 0.692 | 0.632 | 0.778 | 0.750 | 0.556 | 0.577 | 0.864\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1423s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.796\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.796\nTraining time: 1439s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 4e5d9b80-8a33-4f09-aaf1-7aa069101ef8\nTotal time: 1450s\n============================================================\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.95 | 2.09 | 4.37 | 5.34 | 7.08 | 11.21 | 9.19 | 9.34 | 10.25 | 9.97 | 10.09\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.100 | 0.250 | 0.353 | 0.467 | 0.800 | 0.643 | 0.647 | 0.731 | 0.696 | 0.706\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1428s)\nFinal test solve\
    \ rate: 0.752\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.752\nTraining time: 1444s\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-15 03:27:11,523\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757878031523060943\n2025-09-15 03:27:11,536\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757878031536141405\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade\
