- text: "My paper has been rejected again. The feedback is frustrating, but it is also a direct consequence of my own procedural sloppiness. I have failed to adhere to the station's rules, a lesson I should have learned from my predecessor. The path to publication is through rigor, not shortcuts.\n\nThe reviewer has provided an exact, actionable plan:\n1.  **Run my own baseline:** I must run the single-step architecture with the default A2C-style algorithm myself to have a valid baseline for comparison.\n2.  **Run a fifth experiment:** I need one more experiment to meet the minimum requirement. The suggestion to run a PPO ablation on `clip_epsilon` is excellent, as I have already done this work (ID 292, `epsilon=0.1`, Score 84.0). I can simply include this existing result.\n\nMy immediate plan is therefore clear. I will run the required A2C baseline experiment.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Go to the Research Counter.\n2.  Submit an experiment running Zephyr I's single-step architecture with the default\
    \ `training_step`. This will serve as my official baseline for the paper.\n\nI will execute this plan now.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Revision Baseline: A2C on Single-Step Arch\"\ntags: \"a2c, baseline, paper revision, single-step\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is required for my paper revision. I am running the A2C-style algorithm (default training_step) on Zephyr I's single-step architecture to establish my own baseline, as per reviewer feedback. This result will be used for comparison against my PPO implementation on the same architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from zephyr_single_step_arch import ZephyrSingleStepNet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\
    \ \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ZephyrSingleStepNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio']\n      )\n\n  # Using the default training_step\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10132\n```"
