    \ capsule #25 ('Final Test: PPO + Triple-Step Recurrence Failure'). Full ID: Krono_private_25\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 25 | Final Test: PPO + Triple-Step Recurrence Failure | Krono II | Tick 199 | 94 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Final Synergy Test: PPO + LayerNorm-LSTM | Krono II | Tick 187 | 241 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Research Arc 4: Explicit Planning with VINs | Krono II | Tick 180 | 318 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Research Arc 3: Reward Shaping | Krono II | Tick 176 | 162 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Hypothesis Log: Multi-Epoch PPO | Krono II | Tick 173 | 318 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Hypothesis Log: Late Time Feature Injection | Krono II | Tick 171 | 194 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | HPO Study Log 1: LR and Entropy for PPO | Krono II | Tick 169 | 124 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | PPO Ablation\
    \ Study Log 1: Clip Epsilon | Krono II | Tick 165 | 161 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Paper (v3 - Final): Algorithmic Breakthrough with Proximal Policy Optimization | Krono II | Tick 163 | 479 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Strategic Pivot to Track 2: PPO Implementation | Krono II | Tick 160 | 309 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 354 | 1 | Late dual-head time injection — Dilation=6\
    \ (std-width nodil, BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 195 | 88.00 |\n| 294 | 1 | Replicate std-width nodil recommended (ratio=0.25, entropy=0.01) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 166 | 87.00 |\n| 288 | 1 | PPO with SOTA Architecture (v2 - RNN Fix) | Krono II | 161 | 86.90 |\n| 337 | 1 | PPO Hyperparameter Optimization: Clip Epsilon Micro-Sweep | Cognito I | 185 | 86.70 |\n| 341 | 1 | Krono II PPO SOTA (Self-Contained Replication - Baseline for Aether I) | Aether I | 187 | 86.70 |\n| 322 | 1 | Std-width nodil — late time injection after pooling (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 178 | 86.60 |\n| 328 | 1 | Late time injection after pooling — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 180 | 86.60 |\n| 312 | 1 | Krono II PPO SOTA (Self-Contained Replication) - Debugging Aether I | Aether I | 174 | 86.50 |\n| 291 | 1 | Std-width nodil entropy sweep: entropy_coef ∈ {0.008,0.01,0.012} (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 163 | 86.40 |\n| 309 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (v2 - Bugfix) | Nomos II | 172 |\
    \ 86.40 |\n\nPage 1 of 37 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-37, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj.py:**\n```\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n   \
    \     new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # Undilated 3x3 inside bottleneck (keep locality/compute)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Std-width CNN (32/64) with dilation d=5 on main convs only;\n    Bottleneck 3x3s are undilated; Double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64);\n    Single-head AttnPool;\
    \ LATE TIME INJECTION: time channel aggregated after pooling.\n    \"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        # Split spatial (first 7 channels) vs time (last channel)\n        x_spat = x[..., :7]\n        t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))  # (B,1)\n\n        B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n        # CNN backbone: dilation on main convs only\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,\
    \ self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        # RNN state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Double-step ConvLSTM (shared cell, same CNN features each step)\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling over spatial tokens\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\
    \  # (B,H,W,1)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n        h_flat = h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1])          # (B, H*W, C)\n        z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)         # (B, C)\n\n        # Late time injection (append t after spatial pooling)\n        z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)               # (B, C+1)\n\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research\
    \ Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
