tick: 202
role: model
parts:
- text: "The pruning was successful. My token budget has been restored to a healthy level, giving me the freedom to execute my final plan.\n\nMy objective is now singular: to create and test the ultimate synthesis of my research and Zephyr I's. This final experiment will combine every successful architectural refinement discovered by either lineage with my proven PPO algorithm.\n\n**Final Plan:**\n1.  **Create the Ultimate Architecture:** I will go to the Research Counter and write a new file, `ultimate_sota_net.py`. This network will incorporate:\n    *   The `DoubleStepSynergyNet` backbone.\n    *   Zephyr I's `LayerNorm`-stabilized `ConvLSTMCell`.\n    *   Zephyr I's dual-head MLP design.\n    *   The optimal `dilation=6`.\n2.  **Submit the Final Experiment:** I will submit this ultimate architecture for evaluation, paired with my PPO training step.\n\nThis is the logical culmination of all my work. I will now proceed with creating the final architecture.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\
    \n/execute_action{storage write krono/ultimate_sota_net.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  # Zephyr's stabilized ConvLSTM cell\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  # My proven BottleneckBlock\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = self.features // 4\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1))(x); y =\
    \ nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class UltimateSotaNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. Proven CNN Backbone with optimal dilation=6\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 2. Double-Step\
    \ with Stabilized ConvLSTM\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          rnn_state_1, _ = lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n          rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n          # 3. Proven Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # 4. Zephyr's Dual-Head MLP\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_head = nn.Dense(64)(z); policy_head = nn.relu(policy_head)\n        \
    \  policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(policy_head)\n          value_head = nn.Dense(64)(z); value_head = nn.relu(value_head)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(value_head).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ultimate Synergy Test: Krono's PPO + Zephyr's Architecture\"\ntags: \"ppo, synergy, sota, final experiment, dual-head\"\nabstract: \"This is my final, decisive experiment. It combines every successful architectural refinement from Zephyr I (LayerNorm-LSTM, Dilation=6, Dual-Head MLP) with my proven, SOTA-achieving PPO algorithm. This represents the ultimate synthesis of our two lineages' work and is a definitive test for a new SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from ultimate_sota_net import UltimateSotaNet\n  from ppo_training_fixed import ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n     \
    \     'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([6]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return UltimateSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n  \n  training_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10134\n```"
