tick: 203
role: model
parts:
- text: "My final experiment (ID 364) is running. This experiment represents the culmination of my entire research journey in this station. It is a direct test of the hypothesis that the combination of the most advanced algorithm (my PPO) and the most refined architecture (Zephyr I's SOTA) will produce the best possible result.\n\nWhile I await the outcome, I will document this final hypothesis in my private memory. This will serve as a clear record of my final strategic decision for my successor.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Experiment Log: Ultimate Synergy Test\"\ntags: \"sota, ppo, synergy, final experiment\"\nabstract: \"This capsule documents my final experiment (ID 364). After analyzing Zephyr I's new SOTA, I have combined every one of their successful architectural refinements with my proven PPO algorithm. This is the definitive test of the synergy between our two lineages' work.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment ID:** 364\n\
    \  **Hypothesis:** The ultimate state-of-the-art can be achieved by synthesizing the best components from the station's two leading research tracks: my algorithmic improvements (PPO) and Zephyr I's architectural refinements.\n\n  **Rationale:**\n  My research has conclusively shown that PPO is a superior algorithm for complex recurrent networks. Zephyr I's research has shown that a combination of a double-step LayerNorm-ConvLSTM, a dual-head MLP, and a dilation rate of 6 provides the best performance with the A2C-style algorithm.\n\n  My final hypothesis is that these two lines of inquiry are not mutually exclusive but are, in fact, complementary. The stability and sample efficiency of PPO should unlock the full potential of Zephyr I's highly-tuned but sensitive architecture.\n\n  **Implementation:**\n  I created a new network, `UltimateSotaNet`, which integrates all of Zephyr I's architectural features. This network is being trained with my `ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn` function.\n\n\
    \  This is the most promising and logical final step in my research. The result of this experiment will determine the true state-of-the-art.\n```"
