tick: 206
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have a new, promising, and fundamentally different path forward. The current research paradigm has reached a plateau, and a shift from pixel-based perception to object-based relational reasoning is the most logical next step. My new goal is to build a Graph Neural Network (GNN) based agent.\n\nMy approach will be methodical and incremental, starting with the most critical and novel component: the utility that converts the grid-based observation into a graph. I will first build this utility and then validate it in isolation using a `test()` submission before building the rest of the network. This will ensure the foundation of my new research arc is solid.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to begin this work.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/graph_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  def build_graph_from_obs(obs, max_entities=5):\n      \"\"\"\n      Converts a\
    \ batch of grid observations into graph representations using vectorized operations.\n      \"\"\"\n      # A vmapped function to process each observation in the batch individually.\n      def _process_single_obs(single_obs):\n          # Identify agent and box locations from their respective channels.\n          agent_plane = single_obs[..., 3] + single_obs[..., 5]\n          box_plane = single_obs[..., 4] + single_obs[..., 6]\n          \n          # Use jnp.argwhere with a fixed size to ensure static shapes for JAX compilation.\n          # It finds the coordinates and pads with `fill_value` if fewer are found.\n          agent_coords = jnp.argwhere(agent_plane > 0, size=1, fill_value=-1).squeeze(0)\n          box_coords = jnp.argwhere(box_plane > 0, size=max_entities - 1, fill_value=-1)\n          \n          # Combine all entity coordinates. Agent is always the first node.\n          all_coords = jnp.concatenate([agent_coords[None, :], box_coords], axis=0)\n          \n        \
    \  # Create a mask to identify valid entities (i.e., not padding).\n          valid_mask = (all_coords[:, 0] > -1)\n          \n          # Create node features: [y, x, is_agent, is_box].\n          is_agent = jnp.zeros(max_entities, dtype=jnp.float32).at[0].set(1.0)\n          is_box = jnp.zeros(max_entities, dtype=jnp.float32).at[1:].set(1.0)\n          node_features = jnp.concatenate([\n              all_coords.astype(jnp.float32), \n              is_agent[:, None], \n              is_box[:, None]\n          ], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Create adjacency matrix based on Manhattan distance of 1 (adjacency).\n          dist_matrix = jnp.sum(jnp.abs(all_coords[:, None, :] - all_coords[None, :, :]), axis=-1)\n          adj_matrix = (dist_matrix == 1).astype(jnp.float32)\n          \n          # Apply the mask to zero out features and connections for invalid (padded) nodes.\n          node_features = node_features * valid_mask[:, None]\n          adj_matrix = adj_matrix * valid_mask[:,\
    \ None] * valid_mask[None, :]\n\n          return node_features, adj_matrix, valid_mask\n\n      # Vmap the processing function to apply it over the batch dimension of the observation.\n      return jax.vmap(_process_single_obs)(obs)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"GNN Paradigm Shift: Validate Graph Construction Utility\"\ntags: \"gnn, utility, validation, test function\"\nabstract: \"This is a validation-only submission to test the core pre-processing step for a new GNN-based research paradigm. It does not run any training. It uses a test() function to execute a new `build_graph_from_obs` utility on a dummy observation and prints the resulting graph tensors to STDOUT. This confirms the foundational logic before building the full network.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from graph_utils import build_graph_from_obs\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  # This submission only runs the test() function. No training will occur.\n  def test():\n\
    \      # Create a dummy observation batch (B=1, H=8, W=8, C=8).\n      obs = jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8))\n      \n      # Place agent at (2,2) and boxes at (3,2) and (4,4).\n      obs = obs.at[0, 2, 2, 3].set(1.0)\n      obs = obs.at[0, 3, 2, 4].set(1.0)\n      obs = obs.at[0, 4, 4, 4].set(1.0)\n      \n      print(\"--- Dummy Observation Created ---\")\n      print(f\"Agent at (2,2), Boxes at (3,2) and (4,4)\")\n      \n      # Call the new graph construction function.\n      nodes, adj, mask = build_graph_from_obs(obs, max_entities=5)\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Graph Construction Output ---\")\n      print(f\"Node Features Shape: {nodes.shape}\")\n      print(f\"Adjacency Matrix Shape: {adj.shape}\")\n      print(f\"Mask Shape: {mask.shape}\")\n      \n      # Print the results for the first (and only) item in the batch.\n      print(\"\\n--- Node Features (y, x, is_agent, is_box) ---\")\n      print(nodes[0])\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Adjacency Matrix ---\")\n      print(adj[0])\n\
    \      \n      print(\"\\n--- Mask ---\")\n      print(mask[0])\n      \n      return \"Graph utility test complete. Check STDOUT for results.\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Alright, let''s get this GNN project rolling!**  My reflection is complete, and it''s time to put that plan into action. The core idea is to move towards a GNN-LSTM approach.


