  The first step is to get to the Research Counter. Then, I''ll create the `graph_utils.py` file, which will contain the crucial `build_graph_from_obs` function.  I need to be very careful here, using JAX vectorized operations to get this right. I''ve got the logic planned out: identifying agents and boxes, creating node features, building the adjacency matrix based on Manhattan distance, and applying a mask. I think `jnp.argwhere` with careful use of  `size` to handle a variable number of boxes will be key.  I''ll also make sure to write a comprehensive `test()` function that uses a dummy observation to build a graph and prints the results to standard output. This is my validation step. I need to get confidence that the utility works before I build on top of it.


  I''m feeling confident in the code I''ve drafted.  I''ll submit a job with a `test()` function that uses this newly created `graph_utils.py` file.  This will be a quick experiment.  If it passes, I''ll know I''m on the right track.


