tick: 208
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully built and documented the foundational components for my GNN paradigm shift. The `graph_utils` module is validated, and the `gnn_layers` module is implemented. It is now time to assemble these pieces into a complete network and run the first, crucial proof-of-concept experiment.\n\nMy plan, as solidified during my reflection, is to create a `GNN_LSTM_Net` that uses the GNN as a feature extractor for a recurrent LSTM. I will use the default A2C-style algorithm for this initial test to isolate the performance of the architecture itself. The goal is viability, not SOTA. A score above 70% will be a major success.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter, write the full network architecture to a new file, and submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/gnn_lstm_net.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from graph_utils\
    \ import build_graph_from_obs\n  from gnn_layers import GraphAttentionLayer\n\n  class GnnLstmNet(nn.Module):\n      gnn_features: int\n      gnn_layers: int\n      lstm_features: int\n      max_entities: int = 5\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. Graph Construction\n          # Convert the (B, 8, 8, 8) observation into graph tensors.\n          nodes, adj, mask = build_graph_from_obs(x, self.max_entities)\n          \n          # 2. GNN Message Passing\n          # Stack multiple GAT layers to perform relational reasoning.\n          for _ in range(self.gnn_layers):\n              nodes = GraphAttentionLayer(self.gnn_features)(nodes, adj, mask)\n          \n          # 3. Graph Readout\n          # The agent is always the first node. We use its final embedding as the summary of the relational state.\n     \
    \     graph_readout = nodes[:, 0, :]\n          \n          # 4. Recurrent Cell for Temporal Context\n          # Initialize LSTM state if it's the start of an episode.\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = nn.LSTMCell.initialize_carry(\n                  jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (B,), self.lstm_features\n              )\n          # Reset LSTM state for finished episodes.\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y * m, rnn_state)\n          \n          # Pass the graph readout through the LSTM cell.\n          rnn_state, lstm_out = nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_features)(rnn_state, graph_readout)\n\n          # 5. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(lstm_out); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"GNN Paradigm Shift:\
    \ Proof-of-Concept Experiment\"\ntags: \"gnn, lstm, architecture, proof-of-concept\"\nabstract: \"This is the first full test of a new GNN-based paradigm. The agent uses a GNN to build a relational model of the game state, then feeds the result into an LSTM to maintain temporal context. This is a proof-of-concept test using the default A2C-style algorithm. The goal is to prove viability (>70% solve rate), not to achieve a new SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from gnn_lstm_net import GnnLstmNet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'gnn_features': tune.choice([64]), \n          'gnn_layers': tune.choice([3]), \n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return GnnLstmNet(\n          gnn_features=hparams['gnn_features'],\n\
    \          gnn_layers=hparams['gnn_layers'],\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features']\n      )\n  \n  # Using the default training_step to test the architecture in isolation.\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 20230\n```"
